<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">7.3</p>
    <h2 id="t-collapse">Quantum Collapse as Möbius Identification</h2>
    <p>The wavefunction is complex-valued: it has two faces, real and imaginary. Superposition is the
      state in which both faces are simultaneously present &mdash; a two-faced surface. Collapse is the
      <em>identification</em> of those faces: the moment the half-twist completes and both reveal
      themselves as one continuous surface.</p>
    <p class="lede">Quantum collapse is two faces of possibility becoming one face of fact.</p>
    <p class="muted">What this does not do is tell you <em>when</em> collapse happens, or what triggers
      it. It offers a topology for the event, not a dynamics. Any reading that quietly promotes it to a
      solution of the measurement problem has overstated it. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">7.4 &mdash; the chapter's one real prediction-shaped claim</p>
    <h2 id="t-cp">Matter, Antimatter, and the Möbius Berry Phase</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">Why does the universe contain matter rather than equal parts matter and
      antimatter? The laws are nearly symmetric; the measured CP violation is real but far too small to
      account for the imbalance. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="frame illuminated">
      <p>The framework proposes that CP violation is a <strong>Möbius Berry phase</strong>: a geometric
        phase of π acquired by a quantum state traversing the non-contractible loop of the Möbius throat
        that connects the two boundary conditions. Matter acquires phase θ crossing the throat;
        antimatter acquires θ + π, because of the half-twist. The difference of exactly π is the
        structural signature of the topology &mdash; on this reading the asymmetry is not a violation of
        symmetry but its geometric expression. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
      <p>Carried further: if the throat joining zero and one has a half-twist, an object entering one
        mouth emerges from the other as its own mirror image, parity reversed. Matter entering a Möbius
        wormhole emerges as antimatter, and the universe of matter we inhabit may be the Möbius image of
        a complementary antimatter universe on the far side of the throat. Not an asymmetry: a perfect
        symmetry expressed through inversion. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
      <p class="muted">The debt is plain, and the appendix on galaxy handedness pays part of it: a
        geometric phase that is to do real work must be computed, not asserted, and it must say something
        a laboratory could check. That is named as the framework's one genuinely falsifiable edge, and it
        is where a critic should go first.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">7.5</p>
    <h2 id="t-moebius-self">The Möbius Self</h2>
    <p>The ordinary self is a cylinder: two-faced, bounded, with a clear distinction between inside
      &mdash; one's own experience and memory &mdash; and outside. You can trace the edge all the way
      round without inside and outside ever changing places.</p>
    <p>In deep meditation, in mystical states, in certain moments of profound openness, that boundary
      becomes permeable; observer and observed stop being two things. In topological terms the
      experiential surface has taken the half-twist. The cylindrical self has become a Möbius surface,
      and what was outside is now continuous with what was inside.</p>
    <p class="lede">The mystic who says &ldquo;I am the universe&rdquo; is not speaking metaphorically.
      From within a Möbius surface the statement is precisely accurate: inside and outside are the same
      face. <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p class="muted">The difference between ordinary and mystical consciousness, on this reading, is not
      a difference in content but in topology: cylinder or strip, two faces or one.</p>
  </div>
</section>

